---
import { AGENDA } from "../../lib/contact";
import StudioLayout from "../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro";
---
<StudioLayout
  titre={'Working together'}
  description={'From diagnosis to ongoing agent support: our method, our commitments and the scope to agree together.'}
  actif="travailler-ensemble">
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Working together</p>
    <h1>One process at a time, measured at every step.</h1>
    <p class="lead">We start by understanding your processes with your teams and estimating the potential gains. We prepare the information needed, deploy the AI agents, then monitor their operation and results.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>What we commit to</h2>
    <ul class="measures">
      <li>Start with one process, not ten</li>
      <li>Show you what it really brought in, with the figures to back it</li>
      <li>Let you leave with what was built</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="suivi" style="margin-top:2.2em">Support after deployment</h2>
    <p>Ongoing oversight includes monitoring the agents, fixing malfunctions and a quarterly report comparing the real gain with the diagnosis projection.</p>
    <p>If your processes or tools change, the agents may need adapting. The changes needed and their scope are to be agreed together.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:2.2em">What we don&rsquo;t do</h2>
    <ul class="measures">
      <li>Deploy an agent without a prior diagnosis</li>
      <li>Bill AI usage with a hidden margin</li>
      <li>Make you dependent on a component you couldn&rsquo;t take over</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:2em">Pricing is shared after the first conversation, based on the scope agreed.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Let&rsquo;s talk about your scope</h2>
    <p>45 minutes is enough to know whether a diagnosis makes sense for you.</p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href={AGENDA} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
</StudioLayout>
